# Preview only (no recordings, no screenshots)

Yanice reviews this site **only** on the **Cloudflare live preview** (`https://*.trycloudflare.com` → port 4800). This is the sole review surface for every task — not agent-captured video, stills, or desktop/browser recordings.

This rule **overrides** walkthrough-artifacts, RecordScreen, computerUse visual QA, and any “verify in the browser / upload a demo recording” instruction for this repository.

`.cursor/environment.json` installs `cloudflared` and starts an **cloudflare-tunnel** terminal alongside **astro-dev**. Always paste the live tunnel URL; never substitute screenshots or recordings.

## Never

- `RecordScreen` (start, save, or discard)
- Screenshots, screen recordings, or walkthrough artifacts
- `computerUse` / browser automation whose purpose is to capture or prove the UI
- Asking Yanice to watch an agent recording instead of the live site

## Do

- Keep `npm run dev` on port **4800**
- Point Yanice at the live Cloudflare quick tunnel (`*.trycloudflare.com`) that forwards to `http://127.0.0.1:4800`
- If a tunnel terminal is already running, read its log and paste the current `https://*.trycloudflare.com` URL in the reply
- If no tunnel is running, start `$HOME/.local/bin/cloudflared tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:4800` (or `cloudflared` if on PATH) and paste the printed URL — do not then screenshot that URL
- Prove behavior with `npm test`, `curl`, and the preview link — not with media

Astro already allows `*.trycloudflare.com` hosts (`astro.config.mjs`). Production remains Vercel (`yaniceyang.com`); the tunnel is the **working preview** for in-progress work.
